  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_020 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) at 0.6352 acc / 0.6183 F1. PCA-based RNA encoding clearly outperforms scgpt (0.6287 vs 0.5176), multimodal far exceeds image-only (0.63 vs 0.33), and weighted fusion shows a modest edge over concat. Uncertainty: We have only tested avgpool aggregation with this top-performing RNA+image encoder pair; transformer aggregation is unexplored and could better capture inter-profile interactions in the multiprofile setting. This experiment (config_022) changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping the validated best components (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion), making it a clean, minimal exploitation step. With 5 experiments remaining, testing the single most impactful untested dimension (aggregation) on the proven-best backbone is the highest-value use of this slot, as a positive result would establish a new best config to build upon, while a null result would confirm avgpool sufficiency and free remaining budget for other axes (e.g., image encoder or profile setting)."
}

